piece hooks
bpm 128
bars 16

# Four hooks over one groove, four bars each, so they can be judged against
# each other rather than against a memory.
#
#   bars  1-4   pluck      FM, short and bright, on a tresillo
#   bars  5-8   acid       the resonant bass doing what it was built for
#   bars  9-12  stab       supersaw chords on the offbeat, the house organ
#   bars 13-16  layered    the same line on FM and saws an octave apart
#
# A minor throughout. What makes a hook work on a floor, in the order it
# matters: a rhythm you could clap before you could hum it; a gap, because the
# silence is part of the phrase; repetition with exactly one thing changed, so
# the ear learns it by the third time and the fourth pays; and a register
# between the bass and the hats where nothing else is competing.
#
# The tresillo under hook one — 3+3+2, steps 0 3 6 8 11 14 — is the single
# most useful rhythm in dance music and the reason hook one works at all.

# Everything 0.61x: the balance that made the four hooks comparable
# peaked at +2.8 dBFS, and there is still no limiter.
lane kick  clip=floor inst=kick root=A1  gain=0.577 len=0.4s
lane clap  clip=floor inst=hat  root=C-1 gain=0.334 len=0.16s send=0.35
lane hat   clip=floor inst=hat  root=C-1 gain=0.182 len=0.04s send=0.08 orbit=1.1/8/0/0/0/1
lane sub   clip=floor inst=bass root=A0  gain=0.486 len=1.6 duck vel=8

lane pluck clip=hook inst=glass   root=A3 gain=0.577 len=2.2 send=0.3 plays=0-4 vel=8
lane acid  clip=hook inst=bass    root=A1 gain=0.516 len=0.9 duck plays=4-8 vel=8
lane stab1 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.573 len=1.6 send=0.3 plays=8-12 vel=8
lane stab2 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.397 len=1.6 send=0.3 plays=8-12 vel=8
lane stab3 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.312 len=1.6 send=0.35 plays=8-12 vel=8
lane bell  clip=hook inst=glass   root=A4 gain=0.425 len=5 send=0.45 plays=12-16 vel=8
lane under clip=hook inst=strings root=A3 gain=1.446 len=6 send=0.3 plays=12-16 vel=7

